WEBVTT

00:35:28.476 --> 00:35:30.036
than it is in the United States,

00:35:30.076 --> 00:35:32.596
and I think that that's
underappreciated in the West.

00:35:32.636 --> 00:35:34.796
So even though I think there's pressure,

00:35:34.836 --> 00:35:38.796
I really don't think
that it's super likely

00:35:38.836 --> 00:35:42.196
that Putin is out anytime imminently.

00:35:42.236 --> 00:35:46.516
BG: Ed is asking whether you see
any off-ramp for Putin.

00:35:48.036 --> 00:35:54.196
IB: I think that the most likely off-ramp
for Putin is after Kyiv is taken

00:35:54.196 --> 00:35:58.316
and Zelenskyy is removed
one way or the other,

00:35:58.356 --> 00:35:59.516
at that point,

00:35:59.556 --> 00:36:03.596
the possibility of the Russians
accepting a frozen conflict